9. Domiciliary Hospitalization
We will cover the Medical Expenses incurred in respect of Your Domiciliary Hospitalization , subject to
the following conditions::
i. The Domiciliary Hospitalization commenced on the written advice of a Medical Practitioner
and continues for at least 3 consecutive days.
ii. This benefit will not cover the Medical Expenses incurred in respect of Domiciliary
Hospitalization for following:
a. Asthma, bronchitis, tonsillitis, upper respiratory tract infection, including laryngitis and
pharyngitis, cough and cold, and influenza;
